MatchDay

MatchDay is a football-focused web application that provides users with football news, matches, league information, teams, comments, and user profile management.

Technology Stack

Main Application

Java 17
Spring Boot
Spring MVC
Spring Security
Spring Data JPA
Thymeleaf
Spring Cloud OpenFeign
Spring Cache
Spring Scheduling
Maven
MySQL
Lombok
Jakarta Bean Validation
JUnit

REST Microservice

Java 17
Spring Boot
Spring Web
Spring Data JPA
Maven
MySQL

Supported Features

User registration and login
User authentication and authorization
User profile management
Favourite team selection
User role management
Football article browsing
Adding and deleting articles
Adding and viewing article comments
Football match management
League table viewing
Team information
Email notifications
Email preference management
Data validation
Caching
Scheduled tasks

Functionalities

Users can register and log in to the application.
Users can edit their profile information, including their favourite team.
Administrators can manage user roles.
Administrators can add and delete football articles.
Users can browse football articles.
Users can add comments to articles and view comments belonging to an article.
Administrators can add football matches.
Users can view matches and league tables.
Users can view information about football teams and their statistics.
Users can manage their email notification preferences.
The application can send email notifications to users.
The application uses caching to reduce unnecessary requests and improve performance.
The application uses scheduled tasks to perform automated operations.

Integrations

The Main application communicates with the REST microservice through REST APIs using Spring Cloud OpenFeign.
The REST microservice uses a separate MySQL database.
The application integrates with an SMTP mail server for sending emails.
The application uses MySQL for persistent data storage.

REST Microservice

Article and comment functionality is handled by a separate REST microservice.

The REST microservice is available in a separate GitHub repository:

https://github.com/NikolaPenkov06/MatchDayService.git